.Dd 2025-09-30
.Dt CMS_GET0_TYPE 3ossl
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm CMS_get0_type ,
.Nm CMS_set1_eContentType ,
.Nm CMS_get0_eContentType ,
.Nm CMS_get0_content
.Nd get and set CMS content types and content
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.In openssl/cms.h
.Ft const ASN1_OBJECT *
.Fo CMS_get0_type
.Fa "const CMS_ContentInfo *cms"
.Fc
.Ft int
.Fo CMS_set1_eContentType
.Fa "CMS_ContentInfo *cms"
.Fa "const ASN1_OBJECT *oid"
.Fc
.Ft const ASN1_OBJECT *
.Fo CMS_get0_eContentType
.Fa "CMS_ContentInfo *cms"
.Fc
.Ft ASN1_OCTET_STRING *
.Fo *CMS_get0_content
.Fa "CMS_ContentInfo *cms"
.Fc
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Fn CMS_get0_type
returns the content type of a CMS_ContentInfo structure as an
ASN1_OBJECT pointer.
An application can then decide how to process the CMS_ContentInfo
structure based on this value.
.Pp
.Fn CMS_set1_eContentType
sets the embedded content type of a CMS_ContentInfo structure.
It should be called with CMS functions (such as
.Xr CMS_sign 3 ,
.Xr CMS_encrypt 3 )
with the
.Sy CMS_PARTIAL
flag and
.Sy before
the structure is finalised, otherwise the results are undefined.
.Pp
ASN1_OBJECT
.Xr *CMS_get0_eContentType 3
returns a pointer to the embedded content type.
.Pp
.Xr CMS_get0_content 3
returns a pointer to the
.Vt ASN1_OCTET_STRING
pointer containing the embedded content.
.Sh NOTES
As the
.Sy 0
implies
.Fn CMS_get0_type ,
.Fn CMS_get0_eContentType
and
.Xr CMS_get0_content 3
return internal pointers which should
.Sy not
be freed up.
.Fn CMS_set1_eContentType
copies the supplied OID and it
.Sy should
be freed up after use.
.Pp
The
.Sy ASN1_OBJECT
values returned can be converted to an integer
.Sy NID
value using
.Xr OBJ_obj2nid 3 .
For the currently supported content types the following values are
returned:
.Bd -literal
 NID_pkcs7_data
 NID_pkcs7_signed
 NID_pkcs7_digest
 NID_id_smime_ct_compressedData:
 NID_pkcs7_encrypted
 NID_pkcs7_enveloped
.Ed
.Pp
The return value of
.Xr CMS_get0_content 3
is a pointer to the
.Vt ASN1_OCTET_STRING
content pointer.
That means that for example:
.Bd -literal
 ASN1_OCTET_STRING **pconf = CMS_get0_content(cms);
.Ed
.Pp
.Sy *pconf
could be NULL if there is no embedded content.
Applications can access, modify or create the embedded content in a
.Vt CMS_ContentInfo
structure using this function.
Applications usually will not need to modify the embedded content as it
is normally set by higher level functions.
.Sh RETURN VALUES
.Fn CMS_get0_type
and
.Fn CMS_get0_eContentType
return an ASN1_OBJECT structure.
.Pp
.Fn CMS_set1_eContentType
returns 1 for success or 0 if an error occurred.
The error can be obtained from ERR_get_error(3).
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr ERR_get_error 3
